Two options:

Option A — Android Studio (easiest)
cd ManagementDashboard.App
npx cap open android
In Android Studio:
- Debug APK: Build → Build Bundle(s) / APK(s) → Build APK(s) → output in android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
- Release APK: Build → Generate Signed Bundle / APK → APK → you'll need a keystore (create one if you don't have it)

---
Option B — Command line (no Android Studio needed)

Debug APK:
cd ManagementDashboard.App/android
.\gradlew assembleDebug
Output: app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk

Release APK (unsigned, for sideloading):
.\gradlew assembleRelease
Output: app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release-unsigned.apk

---
Before either option, make sure the web assets are current:
cd ManagementDashboard.App
npm run build
npx cap sync android

For sideloading onto your own phone, the debug APK is the quickest path — no signing required, just enable "Install from unknown sources" on the device and transfer the APK.

