You need JDK 17. Quickest path:

1. Install via winget (no browser needed):
winget install Microsoft.OpenJDK.17

2. Set JAVA_HOME (after install):
[System.Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable("JAVA_HOME", "C:\Program Files\Microsoft\jdk-17.0.x.x-hotspot", "Machine")
The exact path will vary — check with:
Get-ChildItem "C:\Program Files\Microsoft" | Where-Object Name -like "jdk-17*"
Use whatever path that returns.

3. Restart your terminal, then verify:
java -version

4. Then build:
cd ManagementDashboard.App/android
.\gradlew assembleDebug

---
Alternatively, if you'd rather use Android Studio, it bundles its own JDK — just run npx cap open android from ManagementDashboard.App/ and let Android Studio handle the build. No manual JDK setup needed.

